{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Let my soul die the death of the upright.</b> If only my soul would die now — provided its death be the death of the upright, so that after it I may merit eternal life." "<b>And let my end be like his.</b> Provided that my end and the offspring of my body be like Israel's, for truly a man's sons and those who issue from his loins are called his end, as in תְּהִי אַחֲרִיתוֹ לְהַכְרִית (Psalms 109:13), and likewise וְלֹא לְאַחֲרִיתוֹ (Daniel 11:4)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:52.952416456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}